  "limitations": [
    "Retrieval coverage: on the ten FR31 scenarios and the cage fixture a candidate run delivers background through the same full-history path as the baseline (run_scenario_turn); the registry index is consulted only for the FR40 scenario. Their observations are byte-identical to the baseline's for every candidate, so those scenarios cannot discriminate backends.",
    "Scoring parity: a candidate run scores all seven FR40 turns while the baseline sweep scores gold-bearing turns only, which is why the two published aggregates differ mostly by scoring set. The gate therefore reads gold_turn_subset/totals, not published_metrics.",
    "Shared candidate state: _run_fr40_scenario builds one index per scenario run and appends the same six record ids once per repetition, so re-appended versions crowd distinct records out of search(limit=6) from repetition 2 on. Candidate FR40 scores therefore depend on run_index (delivered background tokens per reference-turn repetition: 118, 69, 45, 45, 45 for structured/vector-hybrid/embedding; 118, 69, 48, 48, 48 for graph).",
    "Observation keys: turn_index means the position within gold_turns() in the baseline arm and the absolute turn position in the FR40 candidate arm; _canonical_rows normalizes both before comparison.",
    "Latency is the Metric Contract's pinned constant (same value in every arm), so the final tie-breaker carries no discriminating signal here.",
    "The FR21 qualification predicate ('improved correctness/recall') was still without an owner ruling on both readings (strict improvement in both, versus no regression in either plus improvement in one). Both readings are evaluated and reported; the verdict does not depend on which one wins."
  ],
